  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionId": "section-introduction",
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "sourceAnchor": "introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "DnD 5.5’s "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Infernal Dragoon",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/feats/2097451-infernal-dragoon"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " feat, introduced in “D&D Beyond Drops”, gives you a grab bag of magical abilities that are vageuly fiend-themed. The feat doesn’t have a clear mechanical focus, and each of the features are fine individually, but they don’t build toward any specific function, which may make it hard to fit this feat into an optimized build."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-ablity-score-increase",
      "heading": "Ablity Score Increase",
      "sourceAnchor": "ablity-score-increase",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-ablity-score-increase-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Martial characters will mostly choose Constitution, but Charisma can work for some martial builds and for Charisma-based spellcasters. Not including Strength or Dexterity as an option is difficult for many martial characters at the low levels where the feat’s other features are most impactful."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-devilish-aura",
      "heading": "Devilish Aura",
      "sourceAnchor": "devilish-aura",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-devilish-aura-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Fear in a 30-foot emanation with no usage limitation. This is excellent crowd control, and there’s nothing stopping you from using this in every encounter if you find that useful."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-devils-favor",
      "heading": "Devil’s Favor",
      "sourceAnchor": "devils-favor",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-devils-favor-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "+2 is nice, but it’s once per Long Rest, and you need to use it when you make the roll, which means before you see the result of the d20. You essentially need to guess, and then you have a 10% chance for it to matter. There’s a reason that the DnD 5.5 rules updated options like Bardic Inspiraton to apply "
            },
            {
              "type": "emphasis",
              "text": "after"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " you roll the d20."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-diabolic-empowerment",
      "heading": "Diabolic Empowerment",
      "sourceAnchor": "diabolic-empowerment",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-diabolic-empowerment-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Basically a free +1 weapon that works for 8 hours a day. If your game doesn’t include magic weapons, this is fantastic. Gish builds may appreciate this, but every spellcaster with any business using weapons already has Magic Weapon on their spell list."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-diabolic-empowerment-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Even if you’re not planning to use weapons, remember that you can cast Magic Weapon on an ally’s weapon."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-6",
      "heading": "What are DnD Beyond Drops?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-6-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Starting in April of 2026, DnD Beyond Drops aim to release monthly content for DnD 5.5 accessible exclusively to users with a paid subscription to DnD Beyond. The included character options are shareable with subscriptions that allow content sharing. For more information, see the official "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "D&D Beyond Drops FAQ",
              "href": "https://dndbeyond-support.wizards.com/hc/en-us/sections/48937182240404"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ". The developers also posted "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Reddit AMA discussing Drops",
              "href": "https://www.reddit.com/r/dndbeyond/comments/1t6f0pe/ama_with_ddb_executive_producer_drops_product/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " when they were announced."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-6-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "We saw the first round of errata for Drops in "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "August of 2026",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/posts/2222-d-d-beyonds-august-drop-sewers-and-treasures?icid_medium=organic&icid_source=homepage_drops&icid_campaign=2026_drops&icid_content=2026_hype"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", so it appears that WotC plans to continue supporting Drops and to update the published content."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
